{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-34-numerical-methods-applied-to-chemi_syllabus","statement":"The required textbook is Kenneth J. Beers' 'Numerical Methods for Chemical Engineering: Applications in MATLAB,' Cambridge University Press, 2006, ISBN 9780521859714.","source_span":"Required textbook: Beers, Kenneth J. Numerical Methods for Chemical Engineering: Applications in MATLAB. Cambridge University Press, 2006. ISBN: 9780521859714."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-34-numerical-methods-applied-to-chemi_syllabus","statement":"The reference book Press, W.H., 'Numerical Recipes 3rd Edition: The Art of Scientific Computing' (Cambridge University Press, 2007, ISBN 9780521880688), provides short clear synopses of methods for many types of problems.","source_span":"Press, W. H. Numerical Recipes 3rd Edition: The Art of Scientific Computing. Cambridge University Press, 2007. ISBN: 9780521880688... This book provides short clear synopses of methods for many types of problems."}
