{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-37-chemical-and-biological-reaction-e_assignments","statement":"Problem set 8's problem 11-5 contains a typo: the reactor pipe length should be 20 cm, not 20 m.","source_span":"There is a typo in the problem statement for 11-5. The length of the reactor pipe should be 20 cm, not 20 m."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-37-chemical-and-biological-reaction-e_assignments","statement":"For problem set 8, at 500°C the viscosity of hydrogen is 0.015 centipoise and the viscosities of cyclohexane and benzene are both 0.1 centipoise.","source_span":"At 500oC, the viscosity of hydrogen is 0.015 centipoise and the viscosities of cyclohexane and benzene are both 0.1 centipoise."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-37-chemical-and-biological-reaction-e_assignments","statement":"For problem set 8, the diffusivity of all species (Dab) is assumed to be 0.857 cm2/s at the reactor's temperature and pressure.","source_span":"Assume the diffusivity of all species (D ab ) is 0.857 cm 2 /s at the reactor T and P"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-37-chemical-and-biological-reaction-e_assignments","statement":"The WebLab experiment studies the reaction of phenolphthalein in aqueous sodium hydroxide solution, comparing an ideal CSTR model against a non-ideal bypass/dead volume model.","source_span":"A reaction of phenolphthalein occurs in aqueous sodium hydroxide solution."}
